The jumps is a list of -1, -1, -1, 9, -1, -1, -1, -1, -1, and -1.
The visited is a list of 10 zeros.
The distance is a list of 10 zeros.
The queue is an empty list of whole numbers.
Set item 1 of visited to 1.
Place 1 into queue.
The head is 0.
The count is 1.
The target is 9.
Repeat while head is less than count.
The node is item head of queue.
Add 1 to head.
For every roll from 1 to 6.
The landing is node plus roll.
If landing is at most target.
The jump is item landing of jumps.
If jump is not -1, set landing to jump.
If item landing of visited is 0, set item landing of visited to 1, set item landing of distance to item node of distance plus 1, Place landing into queue, add 1 to count.

Show item target of distance.
